{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it came between the camp of Egypt</b> etc. Perhaps the entire expanse of space between the two camps was filled by the cloud and the darkness, and that is what the verse means by <b>and it came between</b> etc. — for otherwise, why was it necessary to say ״וַיָּבֹא בֵּין״ etc., after it already said ״וַיֵּלֶךְ מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶם וַיַּעֲמֹד מֵאַחֲרֵיהֶם״?"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:56.849665346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}